 "<0>Self-consistency</0>: sample N reasoning chains (temperature > {#}), take the majority answer. Errors scatter; correct answers agree.": "",
 "<0>Best-of-N</0>: sample N, let a <1>verifier</1> or reward model pick the best. Works if the checker is reliable.": "",
 "<0>Tree search</0>: expand partial reasoning steps, score them, keep the promising branches.": "",
 "All three trade more inference compute (N× tokens) for accuracy — no retraining needed.": "",
 "Majority vote only helps when each sample is right more often than any single wrong answer; at p ‹ {#} with concentrated errors it can hurt.": "",
 "Gains saturate and samples are correlated in practice, so real curves are flatter than the independent-sample math (hedged).": "",
