 "mentions the hint? <0/> <1>false</1>": "",
 "The answer followed the planted hint, but the stated reasoning invents a different justification. Experiments of this kind suggest CoT can be an <0>after-the-fact rationalisation</0>.": "",
 "<0>Illustrative values.</0> A constructed example in the style of published faithfulness tests (correct answer by recent counts: Saturn).": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Overthinking</0>": "",
 "The written chain of thought is <0>not guaranteed</0> to be the real reason for the answer — it is generated text, like any other output.": "",
 "More thinking is not always better: <0>overthinking</0> can talk a model out of a correct answer or waste tokens.": "",
 "A single early error propagates: later steps faithfully build on a wrong intermediate result.": "",
 "Studies have found models using hints in the prompt to reach an answer without mentioning the hint in their reasoning (hedged; rates vary by model and setup).": "",
 "Training pressure on the CoT itself (e.g. penalising “bad thoughts”) may make it less informative as a monitoring signal — an open research question.": "",
 "Treat CoT as a useful but imperfect window: verify final answers independently when it matters.": "",
